      "writtenOn": "2020-10-02T06:09:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, atomic_and in Zephyr performs pure bitwise \"and\" while our atomic_clear_bits(new)/atomic_clear(old) clears selected bits in the mask.\nActually\n(EC) atomic_clear_bits(\u0026var, mask) \u003d atomic  atomic_and(\u0026var, ~mask) (Zephyr)\n\nThe main goal is not to be named closer to Zephyr, but to avoid collision on naming. \nEC\u0027s atomic_clear(old) !\u003d Zephyr\u0027s atomic_clear\nThe functions work differently so we have to distinguish them.",
